# Bridge

Two dimensions that vary independently (notification *type* × delivery *channel*). Compose them at runtime instead of `OrderConfirmationEmail`, `OrderConfirmationSms`, …

Adapter makes an existing API fit. Bridge is designed up front so **both** sides extend without an N×M class grid.

## Anatomy

- Implementor interface (`NotificationSender.send`).
- Concrete implementors (`EmailSender`, `SmsSender`) — often providers.
- Abstraction holds a sender; refined abstractions supply content.

```ts
export abstract class Notification {
  constructor(protected readonly sender: NotificationSender) {}

  abstract buildSubject(): string;
  abstract buildBody(): string;

  notify(to: string) {
    return this.sender.send(to, this.buildSubject(), this.buildBody());
  }
}

export class OrderConfirmationNotification extends Notification {
  constructor(sender: NotificationSender, private readonly orderId: string) {
    super(sender);
  }

  buildSubject() {
    return `Order Confirmation - #${this.orderId}`;
  }

  buildBody() {
    return `Thank you for order #${this.orderId}.`;
  }
}
```

Wire at the edge (workflow / service), not inside the abstraction:

```ts
const sender = this.senders[channel];
const notification =
  type === 'shipping'
    ? new ShippingUpdateNotification(sender, orderId)
    : new OrderConfirmationNotification(sender, orderId);
return notification.notify(to);
```

## Nest mapping

Senders can be singleton providers (SMTP client). Abstractions that close over `orderId` are **plain classes** created per call — do not register them as singletons.

Future media backends (local disk vs object storage) behind `MediaStorageService` is Bridge **if** high-level operations and storage drivers both grow. If there is only one driver, a single service is enough.

## When to use

- Two (or more) independent axes; combinatorial subclasses would explode.
- Swap implementation at runtime (user prefers SMS).

## When not to use

- One axis of variation → Strategy or a single interface.
- Abstraction and implementation always change together.

Related: `nest-adapter.mdc`, `nest-strategy.mdc`, `nest-abstract-factory.mdc`.
